Chapter: CapManifestDerived

 Positive guard for capability stage 3 (formerly the
 cap-launder-manifest probe): opening declares a real I/O effect and
 the binary now ships with a DERIVED capability manifest. The emitter
 collects opening's effect names into the effects section and grants
 each effect's covering capability in the capabilities section, both
 appended inside the hashed and signed content (X86_64Chapter,
 Capability Manifest section). This program's manifest therefore
 carries the Console effect and a Console capability entry; the
 verifier's capability and effect phases (CdxVerifier) decode them
 through the header offsets and are no longer vacuous. Stage 4 wires
 the verified loader's grant bitmask into the kernel process table.

Section: Definitions

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni "capability manifest derived from opening effects"
  end

